WEBVTT

00:30:29.496 --> 00:30:33.996
the most common name. Fast
forward to 2013.

00:30:35.121 --> 00:30:39.621
And now it's one out of seventy
five boys receive

00:30:39.621 --> 00:30:41.538
the most common name of their birth year,

00:30:44.329 --> 00:30:48.829
if you take this idea of increasing
communal orientation,

00:30:48.829 --> 00:30:50.954
decreasing individualism seriously,

00:30:51.288 --> 00:30:54.413
would you also anticipate that we're
going to see more caring

00:30:54.746 --> 00:30:58.996
and more supportive work relationships
in the next couple of decades?

00:30:59.538 --> 00:31:03.079
The findings that I have looked
at suggests that, yes, right.